 - open source load testing tool
 - define how you want to test

current version - 1.4.3
 swarm - group of animals that aggregate and travel in same direction
 hatching - production
 spawn - release new

 - Comes with distributed node(no setup needed like Jmeter)
 - supports multiple protocols


 User class - Represents a user which is to be spawned and attack the system - greenlet
 locust works with Flask UI

 locust -f filename.py --hostname

 TaskSet is and advanced feature
 structure the hierarchical
 can be nested

 Wait time or think time
 helps to simulate real world scenarios


 commands
 -> locust -h
 # for automated testing in jenkins
 -> locust -f file_name.py -u 1 -r 1 -t 10s --headless --csv run.csv --csv-full-history --print-stats --host=https://example.com
 -> -L CRITICAL --logfile mylog.log --html Run1
 -> -l list of classes
 -> --show-task-ratio
 -> --only-summary
 -> --tags get

 User and taskset has on_start and on_stop methods
 these methods will be executed only once

 Correlation
 - extracting the dynamic values from the response
 - pass the extracted value in the subsequent requests
 - session id, order number

 Configuration
 - configuration can be stored inside .conf or yaml files this has highest prio
 - --config configuration file or yaml files

 Events
 we can do tasks at certain circumstances using the event hooks